# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Acetylene: C-C 1.203 A, C-H 1.063 A, linear.
# Geometry: NIST CCCBDB experimental (Angstrom converted at 1 A = 1.8897261 Bohr); the experimental geometry, not this
# solver's minimum (LSDA on a grid relaxes it slightly: press Relax to see where).
# A 16 Bohr box at h = 0.15 (the app's default grid) under the default ionic potential.
grid 107 0.15
charge 0
ionic accepted
nucleus 1 -3.1454 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 6 -1.1367 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 6 1.1367 0.0000 0.0000
nucleus 1 3.1454 0.0000 0.0000
